    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n#42050 fixed `rx` with a multicursor under the primary one, so it wouldn't cause two edits. However, on large buffers, you can see the other cursor snap to the next character as the extmark is moved - and then immediately disappears.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI asked about this on Matrix before making an issue, since I thought it might be WAI. justinmk mentioned:\n> it's because the primary-overlapping cursor is \"healed\" at the end of the action, so it might appear out of sync during cascade. there might be a way to make this look nicer\n> ...\n> probably could disable highlighting on the cursor-overlapping extmark, that's an easy cosmetic fix (but the extmark itself will still be incorrect during cascade). issue welcome\n\nWhich seems like a good-enough fix to me.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-25T14:22:19Z",
